---
title: Peking duck pizza
tags: [duck, weekend]
source: Peking Duck Pizza by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/peking-duck-pizza
---

> A restaurant batch: the dough, duck and chile oil make far more than one pizza.
> Start the dough two days ahead.

== Dough ==

In a #stand mixer{} with the dough hook, put the @flour{700%g},
@olive oil{54%g}, @sugar{30%g}, @salt{17%g}, @active dry yeast{3%g} and
@water{435%g}.

Mix ~{4%minutes} on low, scrape the bowl, mix ~{2%minutes} on high, scrape
again, then mix ~{6%minutes} on low.

Put the dough in a greased bowl, cover, and leave ~{2%hours} at room
temperature.

Press out the air, shape into a ball on a floured counter, wrap tightly and
refrigerate ~{24%hours}. The next day, divide into 500 g balls and keep them
cold.

== Braised duck ==

Heat the oven to 350°F. Lay the @duck legs{5%lb} in a #roasting pan{}.

Heat a little @neutral oil{} in a #stockpot{} over medium heat. Add the
@ginger{1%cup}(diced), @garlic{1%cup}(peeled cloves) and
@scallions{1%bunch}(sliced) and cook until the ginger starts to brown.

Add the @soy sauce{6%cup}, @sugar{3.5%cup}, @cinnamon sticks{5%g},
@Sichuan peppercorns{5%g}, @coriander seeds{5%g}, @whole cloves{6},
@star anise{3%pods} and @water{20%cup}. Bring to a simmer.

Pour the liquid over the duck, cover tightly with foil and a lid, and braise
~{2.5%hours}.

Cool the duck in the liquid. Pick the meat off the bones, moisten it with a
little of the braising liquid, and refrigerate.

== Chile oil ==

Put the @gochugaru{40%g}, @Sichuan peppercorns{30%g} and
@red pepper flakes{25%g} in a heatproof container.

Heat the @neutral oil{750%g} to 350°F in a #saucepan{} and pour it over the
chiles. Let it cool, then strain through a #fine-mesh sieve{}.

== Chile oil vinaigrette ==

Whisk 500 g of the chile oil with the @black vinegar{200%g},
@soy sauce{90%g}, @sesame oil{25%g}, @sugar{20%g} and
@Maggi seasoning{15%g}. Refrigerate.

== Pizza ==

Press one dough ball into a greased #13x9-inch baking dish{}, cover, and leave
~{3%hours} at room temperature. Push the dough into the corners and leave
~{1%hour} more, then push it into the corners again.

Heat the oven to 500°F. Cover the dough with @mozzarella{3%cups}(shredded) and
bake ~{4%minutes}, turn the dish, and bake ~{4%minutes} more until golden. Let
it cool.

Spread @hoisin sauce{} over the crust and top with 2 cups of the braised duck,
more @mozzarella{}(shredded) and a little more hoisin.

Bake ~{10%minutes}, until bubbling and browned on top. Lift it out and cut into
6 pieces.

Finish with @cilantro{}(leaves), @fried shallots{}, @parmesan{}(shaved) and a
drizzle of the chile oil vinaigrette.
